.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH OS8PKG 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
os8pkg \- install OS/8 software packages onto a disk image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B os8pkg
.RI [ options "] [" command "] [" package ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B os8pkg
is the package manager for the OS/8 media shipped with this package.
It reads package descriptions
.RI ( pspec
files) and installs their outputs onto a target RK05 image, the
runtime disk by default. Building packages from their OS/8 sources
also exists (the
.B build
command), but it needs the source tree layout
.RI ( pspec/
and
.IR scripts/misc/ )
that this RPM does not ship; installing prebuilt packages works.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-target " image"
target image file (default
.IR v3d.rk05 )
.TP
.BI \-\-destdir " dir"
destination directory for output files
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
print what would happen; generate no files
.TP
.B \-v
increase output verbosity
.TP
.BI \-d " N"
set debug level
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
install
.I pspec
outputs onto the target image
.TP
.B uninstall
delete
.I pspec
outputs and cleanups from the target image
.TP
.B verify
verify the fidelity of packages installed on the target image
.TP
.B conflicts
report outputs that exist in multiple
.I pspec
files
.TP
.B format
display the output format for the given package names
.TP
.B deps
create a make-style dependency file from inputs
.TP
.B include
create an include script from selected scripts
.TP
.B build
run the package builder (needs the unbuilt source tree)
.TP
.B all
perform all of the above
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/lib/pidp8i/media/os8/
the images packages are installed onto (group-writable)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR os8-run (1),
.BR os8-cp (1),
.BR dnf (8)
(and
.I doc/os8pkg.md
under
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/ )
